</strong></summary><br>

<b>Description:</b> <code>console.error("Failed to parse GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_JSON...", e)</code> may leak sensitive <br>credential material into logs if parsing fails (e.g., malformed <br><code>GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_JSON</code> content or error details containing parts of the secret), <br>creating a risk of credential exposure via application logging.<br> <strong><a href='https://github.com/invidias-codem/ai-saas/pull/31/files#diff-2a2b44b3ec24704da8c8e73dcc52c5c9880132ac5b81a010080781a38a6ebea2R31-R41'>reactLoop.ts [31-41]</a></strong><br>

<details open><summary>Referred Code</summary>

```typescript
// Parse credentials from env if available
const keyJson = process.env.GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_JSON;
let googleAuthOptions;
if (keyJson) {
    try {
        const credentials = JSON.parse(keyJson);
        googleAuthOptions = { credentials };
    } catch (e) {
        console.error("Failed to parse GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_KEY_JSON for Vertex AI auth", e);
    }
}
```

</details></details></td></tr>
